    "2009": {
      "season": 2009,
      "seasonId": "2009",
      "startDate": "2009-06-06",
      "endDate": "2009-10-09",
      "regularSeasonGamesPerTeam": 34,
      "regularSeasonTeamGameSlots": 442,
      "numTeams": 13,
      "isCbaSeason": false,
      "flags": {
        "isCbaSeason": false,
        "isExpansionYear": false,
        "hasFoldedTeams": true,
        "hasRelocations": false,
        "hasDispersalDraft": true,
        "hasExpansionDraft": false,
        "hasCollegeDraft": true,
        "hasPlayoffs": true,
        "hasRegularSeasonAwards": true
      },
      "specialSeasonType": null,
      "notes": "December 1, 2008 Houston Comets folded -> 2009 was first season without the Houston Comets -> dispersal draft was held on December 8, 2008 -> existing teams were picking players for the 2009 season -> so this dispersal draft is labeled as the 2009 Dispersal Draft\n\nOn August 10, 2009, Los Angeles Sparks center Lisa Leslie recorded her 6,000th career point in her team's win against the Indiana Fever. Leslie was the first player in WNBA history to reach the 6,000 point plateau.\n\nThe Phoenix Mercury shot 85.5% from the free-throw line. This clip is the best team free-throw percentage in WNBA and NBA history.\n\nOn September 25, 2009, NBA legend Larry Bird purchased about 9,000 balcony tickets to the Indiana Fever vs. Detroit Shock game three of the Eastern Conference Finals. The tickets were then distributed at the Fever box office free-of-charge to fans. Bird had the sole intent of filling the arena to support the Fever, who had never advanced to the WNBA Finals. Announced attendance at the game was 18,165 and the Fever beat the Shock.\nOn September 28, 2009, Phoenix Suns general manager Steve Kerr purchased about 7,000 balcony tickets to the Phoenix Mercury vs. Indiana Fever game one of the 2009 WNBA Finals. The tickets were then distributed at the Mercury box office free-of-charge to fans. Kerr wanted to follow up Bird's similar action stating that he knows how important a large crowd can be in a Finals series.",
